# Root build-context ignore file.
#
# Several images build from the REPO ROOT context (`docker build -f <svc>/Dockerfile .`)
# because they COPY shared packages/ alongside the service: workflow-recipes,
# control-api, control-ui, profile-ui, host-context-controller,
# packages/workflow-sdk and (since R4/B2) mcp-host. Docker only honors the
# .dockerignore at the CONTEXT root, so the per-service .dockerignore files are
# inert for those builds — this file restores their exclusions globally. Keep
# it in sync with the per-service files (which still apply to any image built
# from its own dir).
#
# SECURITY: without this file the entire monorepo — including real .env files
# and .git history — is shipped to the Docker daemon as build context on every
# root-context build (shared BuildKit runners, CI context tarballs, exported
# caches). None of it is COPY'd into images (all COPYs are narrow), but the
# context itself must not carry secrets.
.git
.specs
.claude
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Credential material that must never enter the build context (no image COPYs
# any of these — verified no tracked *.pem/*.key/kubeconfig* exists in-tree).
**/*.pem
**/*.key
kubeconfig*
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage
**/*.log
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
